<title>PERU: Lima bolsa suspends trade as shrs slide on crisis.</title>
<headline>Lima bolsa suspends trade as shrs slide on crisis.</headline>
<dateline>LIMA 1996-12-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Peru's stock market announced shortly after 1300 local time/1300 EST/1800 GMT it had suspended trading due to heavy losses on the ongoing hostage crisis.</p>
<p>Officials at the bolsa told Reuters the takeover of the Japanese ambassador's house by communist guerrillas was having too heavy an effect on trading.</p>
<p>The General Index had lost 4.43 percent to 1,986.0 points, while the blue-chip Selective Index slid 3.58 percent to 1,397.2 points.</p>
<p>-- Andrew Cawthorne, Lima newsroom, 511 221-2134</p>
